+We give quantitative density theorems for scalar realizations of
+primitive affine companion groups in characteristic two.
+For $t=2^s$, $s\ge2$, and $d=(t+1)(t^2+1)$, let $C_d$ be the
+norm-one subgroup of $\mathbb F_{t^4}^{\times}$.
+The number of slopes $a,1+a\in C_d$ generating $C_d$ is
+$\theta_2(d)(t+1)^2+O(t^{3/2}2^{\omega(d)})$, where
+$\theta_2(d)=\prod_{p\mid d}(1-p^{-2})$.
+The number for which both slopes have order $d$ is asymptotic to
+$(\varphi(d)/d)^2(t+1)^2$, with an explicit error and a sufficient
+condition for existence. These statements concern the full parameter
+family; a fixed norm fiber has size $O(t)$ and a norm-dependent density.
+The proof constructs a geometrically connected product Lang cover of
+genus-one norm fibers, classifies constant norm-character exceptions,
+and proves a uniform mixed-character bound $8\sqrt t$ with tame
+conductor at most eight.
+Separately, exact finite certificates complete an all-dimensional
+existence theorem with one slope of order $d$; double full-order
+existence is proved for all sufficiently large $s$.
+For an affine complete mapping $f(x)=Mx\oplus c$, we determine
+$\langle f,F(f)\rangle=\mathbb F_2[M]c\rtimes
+\langle M,(I+M)^{-1}\rangle$, where
