+Scalar realization estimates and norm-descent obstructions show
+that the uniform index exponent $1/4$ is optimal.
+The operator satisfies $F^3=\mathrm{id}$; its fixed maps correspond
+to oriented line spreads, for which we give conjugacy counts and a
+standard-spread asymptotic. A nonlinear four-dimensional example
+generates $A_{16}$. Specified triality and field-Singer statements
+are checked in Lean; the density results have paper proofs using
+classical curve bounds.
